{"parentUuid":"d3ce34b6-d595-4554-ae46-8e07337c0875","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a0d2d950c3bbd8398","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Fe3NNumcqYR5cwDGiWtsn","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"memetic algorithm 2D rectangle packing problem 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A new heuristic algorithm for rectangle packing | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/222136984_A_new_heuristic_algorithm_for_rectangle_packing\"},{\"title\":\"A New Memetic Algorithm for the Two-Dimensional Bin-Packing Problem with Rotations | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-14883-5_69\"},{\"title\":\"An effective evolutionary algorithm for packing rectangles into a fixed size circular container - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0377221725003297\"},{\"title\":\"A New Memetic Algorithm for the Two-Dimensional Bin-Packing Problem with Rotations | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221611129_A_New_Memetic_Algorithm_for_the_Two-Dimensional_Bin-Packing_Problem_with_Rotations\"},{\"title\":\"Intelligent Algorithms for Rectangular Packing Problem | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-981-19-5916-5_2\"},{\"title\":\"Solving 2D Rectangle Packing Problem Based on Layer Heuristic and Genetic Algorithm | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/6305756/\"},{\"title\":\"Heuristics for Solving the 2D Rectangle Packing Area Minimization Problem Basing on a Dynamic Reduction Method | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/267472609_Heuristics_for_Solving_the_2D_Rectangle_Packing_Area_Minimization_Problem_Basing_on_a_Dynamic_Reduction_Method\"},{\"title\":\"A memetic algorithm for two-dimensional multi-objective bin-packing with constraints | Proceedings of the 13th annual conference companion on Genetic and evolutionary computation\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/2001858.2002016\"},{\"title\":\"Optimizing 2D irregular packing via image processing and computational intelligence | Scientific Reports\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-97202-0\"},{\"title\":\"An Algorithm for Two-Dimensional Cutting Problems | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/opre.25.1.30\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about memetic algorithms applied to 2D rectangle packing problems in 2024-2025:\n\n## Recent Research (2024-2025)\n\nRecently in 2024, Zhang et al. proposed a variable neighborhood search algorithm (denoted by SL-VNS) for the orthogonal packing of rectangles in a circular container problem. This algorithm integrates a skyline-based decoding procedure and several mutation operators, achieving high performance compared to previous heuristic algorithms, especially for large instances.\n\nA 2025 publication in Scientific Reports presented a method for optimizing 2D irregular packing via image processing and computational intelligence.\n\n## Memetic Algorithm Applications\n\nThe memetic algorithm for 2D rectangular strip packing problems hybrids genetic algorithm with Tabu search. Memetic algorithms have been developed to solve 2D bin-packing problems with operators specially designed for this problem.\n\nMemetic Algorithms are population-based meta-heuristic search methods inspired by Darwinian principles of natural selection and Dawkins' notion of meme that have successfully been applied to single- and multi-objective optimization problems.\n\n## Problem Scope\n\nRectangle packing and cutting problems are a class of popular combinatorial optimization problems with important real-world applications, whose goal is to orthogonally pack a set of given rectangles into a container without overlapping.\n\nThe research demonstrates ongoing interest in hybrid metaheuristic approaches like memetic algorithms for solving complex 2D rectangle packing problems efficiently.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"65220109-ce37-4070-995d-b31dd3bb3d68","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:35.172Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d3ce34b6-d595-4554-ae46-8e07337c0875","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a2cea1ac-99ec-42a4-abb2-d8136e3d698a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a0d2d950c3bbd8398","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P4hZBhS4qAKtWjgyTZUS9h","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"genetic algorithm CP-SAT hybrid 2D packing placement constraint programming\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Optimizing Two-Dimensional Irregular Packing: A Hybrid Approach of Genetic Algorithm and Linear Programming | MDPI\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3417/13/22/12474\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ktnr/BinPacking2D: Exact solutions for two-dimensional bin packing problems by branch-and-cut · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ktnr/BinPacking2D\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - johnMinelli/CP-SAT-SMT_2D-StripPacking: 2D Strip Packing problem solved with different approaches\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/johnMinelli/CP-SAT-SMT_2D-StripPacking\"},{\"title\":\"Hybrid-biased genetic algorithm for packing unequal rectangles into a fixed-size circle | Computers and Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1016/j.cor.2024.106716\"},{\"title\":\"A new metaheuristic genetic-based placement algorithm for 2D strip packing | Journal of Industrial Engineering International\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s40092-014-0047-9\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Packing of 2D Irregular Parts: A Hybrid Approach Incorporating a Modified Genetic Algorithm and Image Processing\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2227-7390/12/22/3470\"},{\"title\":\"Hybrid genetic algorithms for constrained placement problems | IEEE Journals & Magazine | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/687887/\"},{\"title\":\"Yet Another Math Programming Consultant: 2d bin packing with Google OR-Tools CP-SAT, how to fix?\",\"url\":\"http://yetanothermathprogrammingconsultant.blogspot.com/2021/02/2d-bin-packing-with-google-or-tools-cp.html\"},{\"title\":\"A new approach for bin packing problem using knowledge reuse and improved heuristic | Scientific Reports\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-024-81749-5\"}]\n\nHere are the search results for your query on genetic algorithm CP-SAT hybrid approaches for 2D packing placement with constraint programming:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**Hybrid Approaches:**\nHeuristic algorithms, including greedy algorithms, simulated annealing algorithms, and genetic algorithms, have demonstrated the capability to yield satisfactory solutions within a limited timeframe, with genetic algorithms being specifically designed to address challenges posed by two-dimensional regular and irregular bin packing problems.\n\n**CP-SAT and Constraint Programming Integration:**\nSolutions can be found during the constructive phase by constraint programming (solving a 2D-BPP with google's CP-SAT solver) or by branch-and-cut. Subproblems are generated and solved by constraint programming (CP) using google or-tools.\n\n**Hybrid Genetic Algorithm Methods:**\nGiven that the 2D-strip packing problem is a complex NP-hard combinatorial optimization, a heuristic based on genetic algorithm can solve it, with hybrid approaches combining genetic encoding and evolution scheme with proposed placement approaches resulting in better population evolution and faster solution convergence to optimal.\n\n**Recent Developments:**\nHybrid methods combine a novel placement procedure with a biased random-key genetic algorithm (BRKGA) for 2D non-guillotine cutting problems. Classic packing solutions use hybrid algorithms based on heuristic positioning and meta-heuristic sequencing.\n\nThe search results indicate that hybrid approaches combining genetic algorithms with constraint programming solvers like CP-SAT are actively being researched for 2D packing and placement problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"620c86c3-4c7e-4e43-b381-a772e08e7202","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:36.235Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a2cea1ac-99ec-42a4-abb2-d8136e3d698a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0261b2b1-5dca-4751-ad52-ac80cbe3c5d1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a0d2d950c3bbd8398","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017LmZhpey3RzxKtHT55FiJS","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"sequence pair encoding genetic algorithm VLSI floorplan 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"An adaptive genetic algorithm for VLSI floorplanning based on sequence-pair | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/855997/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A Genetic Algorithm for VLSI Floorplanning\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220701789_A_Genetic_Algorithm_for_VLSI_Floorplanning\"},{\"title\":\"A Genetic Algorithm for VLSI Floorplanning | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/3-540-45356-3_66\"},{\"title\":\"A Genetic Algorithm for VLSI Floorplanning\",\"url\":\"https://users.cs.cf.ac.uk/C.L.Mumford/papers/ppsn6.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"A Hybrid Reinforcement Learning and Genetic Algorithm for VLSI Floorplanning\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/373763040_A_Hybrid_Reinforcement_Learning_and_Genetic_Algorithm_for_VLSI_Floorplanning\"},{\"title\":\"Genetic Algorithms In VLSI Floorplanning\",\"url\":\"https://www.ijert.org/research/genetic-algorithms-in-vlsi-floorplanning-IJERTV1IS8662.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Improved genetic algorithm for VLSI floorplan design with non-slicing structure - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0360835206000489\"},{\"title\":\"A Deep Reinforcement Learning Floorplanning Algorithm Based on Sequence Pairs\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3417/14/7/2905\"},{\"title\":\"New perspectives in VLSI design automation: deterministic packing by Sequence Pair\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/spr/annopr/v179y2010i1p35-5610.1007-s10479-008-0460-9.html\"},{\"title\":\"A Genetic Algorithm for VLSI Floorplanning | Proceedings of the 6th International Conference on Parallel Problem Solving from Nature\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.5555/645825.668940\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about sequence pair encoding, genetic algorithms, and VLSI floorplanning:\n\n## Key Research Areas\n\nAn adaptive genetic algorithm (GA) has been proposed to solve the floorplanning problem in VLSI layout design, using sequence-pair representation as the coding scheme of each chromosome.\n\nThe sequence-pair approach represents each packing as a pair of module name sequences. Sequence Pair (SP) encoding represents the floorplan structure and leverages algorithms' ability to learn autonomously and generalize to perform floorplanning.\n\n## Recent Developments\n\nThe field has evolved significantly with newer approaches. A deep reinforcement learning floorplanning algorithm based on sequence pairs (SP) has been proposed to address the placement problem, where reinforcement learning utilizes an agent to explore the search space in sequence pairs to find the optimal solution. Experimental results on international standard test circuit benchmarks (MCNC and GSRC) demonstrate that the proposed deep reinforcement learning floorplanning algorithm based on sequence pairs can produce superior solutions.\n\n## Problem Characteristics\n\nFrom a computational perspective, VLSI floorplanning is an NP-hard problem, making it difficult to be efficiently solved by classical optimization techniques. Chromosome encoding in some approaches is based on Sequence Pair, with mutation and local search operators based on swap, reflection/rotation, insertion and reversal perturbations.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5659d258-f0f6-498d-bb84-0e3e281f7c59","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:36.923Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0261b2b1-5dca-4751-ad52-ac80cbe3c5d1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8be34639-e61e-48fc-99ff-8f394a9ef30f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a0d2d950c3bbd8398","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012aP9wswHSB2LDu7NvZ81GJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"island model parallel genetic algorithm facility layout placement large scale\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"On GPU Implementation of the Island Model Genetic Algorithm for Solving the Unequal Area Facility Layout Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3417/8/9/1604\"},{\"title\":\"An island model genetic algorithm for unequal area facility layout problems - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0957417416305358\"},{\"title\":\"Application of Layered Coding Genetic Algorithm in Optimization of Unequal Area Production Facilities Layout - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6607717/\"},{\"title\":\"A genetic algorithm for facility layout problems - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0951524098000184\"},{\"title\":\"An island model genetic algorithm for unequal area facility layout problems | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/309199610_An_island_model_genetic_algorithm_for_unequal_area_facility_layout_problems\"},{\"title\":\"On GPU Implementation of the Island Model Genetic Algorithm for Solving the Unequal Area Facility Layout Problem – DOAJ\",\"url\":\"https://doaj.org/article/9bb442e294134d2eba49ccbe782efe3c\"},{\"title\":\"HOPE: A genetic algorithm for the unequal area facility layout problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054897001007\"},{\"title\":\"A robust Island Parallel Genetic Algorithm for the Quadratic Assignment Problem: International Journal of Production Research: Vol 51, No 14\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/00207543.2012.746798\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) On GPU Implementation of the Island Model Genetic Algorithm for Solving the Unequal Area Facility Layout Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/327567354_On_GPU_Implementation_of_the_Island_Model_Genetic_Algorithm_for_Solving_the_Unequal_Area_Facility_Layout_Problem\"},{\"title\":\"Multi-dimensional resource placement algorithm based on parallel genetic algorithm - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0140366425001926\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about island model parallel genetic algorithms for facility layout placement in large-scale problems:\n\n## Overview\n\nAn Island Model Genetic Algorithm (IMGA) has been proposed to solve unequal area facility layout problems (UA-FLP). The parallel evolution of several populations is used to maintain the population diversity and to obtain a wider sampling of the search space to obtain better quality solutions in fewer generations.\n\n## Problem Context\n\nUnequal area facility layout problems are widely used in different fields, including industrial facility design, warehouse organization, school facility layout, and VLSI element placement. However, UA-FLP is an NP-hard problem, and with the increase in the problem size, the amount of calculation will become larger and larger, and the execution time is getting longer and longer even though metaheuristic approaches such as GA are applied.\n\n## Algorithm Benefits\n\nIMGA is one of the most promising variants among the parallelized models of GA, and can explore different regions of the search space. The proposed approach is able to reach good solutions with a wide range of problem sizes and in a reasonable computational time.\n\n## GPU Acceleration\n\nGPU computing can not only speed up the search process, but also exploit parallelism to improve the quality of the obtained solutions. For practical implementation, a GPU-based approach can increase the speedup to 27x over serial CPU, 4.5x over the traditional island model.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5c613547-a6ae-43ff-bf39-a29a4aa813f0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:37.755Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8be34639-e61e-48fc-99ff-8f394a9ef30f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
