{"parentUuid":"8e6734dc-2db3-4154-98ac-aeb00186550a","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a0d2d950c3bbd8398","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_014sGjUbwXMtC5yvbi2HEVwg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GYDrSoUQvWC1QX2fDwo4Ga","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"genetic algorithm\" rectangle placement 70x70 grid scale \"266\" OR \"200 facilities\" feasibility"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6341,"cache_read_input_tokens":33076,"output_tokens":215,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6341},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":215,"cache_read_input_tokens":33076,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6341,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6341,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosP3DaU7wxfEFxiDM8U","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"6e98e197-7af6-4197-943b-c2c4d744cb5f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:08.179Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8e6734dc-2db3-4154-98ac-aeb00186550a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a0d2d950c3bbd8398","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YHN8dwdsauNWz9bw8eD281","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"BRKGA review 2024 European Journal Operational Research Resende multi-population\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Biased random-key genetic algorithms: A review\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/eee/ejores/v321y2025i1p1-22.html\"},{\"title\":\"Biased random-key genetic algorithms: A review - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0377221724002303\"},{\"title\":\"[2312.00961] Biased Random-Key Genetic Algorithms: A Review\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.00961\"},{\"title\":\"A biased random‐key genetic algorithm for the minimization of open stacks problem - Gonçalves - 2016 - International Transactions in Operational Research - Wiley Online Library\",\"url\":\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1111/itor.12109\"},{\"title\":\"The Multi-Parent Biased Random-Key Genetic Algorithm with Implicit Path-Relinking and its real-world applications | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/337442705_The_Multi-Parent_Biased_Random-Key_Genetic_Algorithm_with_Implicit_Path-Relinking_and_its_real-world_applications\"},{\"title\":\"A parallel multi-population biased random-key genetic algorithm for a container loading problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054811000827\"},{\"title\":\"A parallel multi-population biased random-key genetic algorithm for a container loading problem | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220471603_A_parallel_multi-population_biased_random-key_genetic_algorithm_for_a_container_loading_problem\"},{\"title\":\"Early years of biased random-key genetic algorithms: a systematic review | Journal of Global Optimization | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10898-024-01446-5\"},{\"title\":\"Biased Ranom-Key Genetic Algorithms | Proceedings of the 2016 on Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference Companion\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1145/2908961.2926996\"},{\"title\":\"Biased random-key genetic algorithms with applications in telecommunications | TOP | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11750-011-0176-x\"}]\n\nI found search results for your query. Here's what I discovered about the BRKGA review:\n\nThe review \"Biased random-key genetic algorithms: A review\" was published by Londe, Pessoa, Andrade, and Resende in 2025 in the European Journal of Operational Research, Volume 321(1), pages 1-22.\n\nThe paper is a comprehensive literature review of Biased Random-Key Genetic Algorithms (BRKGA), which is a metaheuristic that employs random-key-based chromosomes with biased, uniform, and elitist mating strategies in a genetic algorithm framework.\n\nThe review encompasses over 150 papers with a wide range of applications, including classical combinatorial optimization problems, real-world industrial use cases, and non-orthodox applications such as neural network hyperparameter tuning in machine learning.\n\nScheduling is by far the most prevalent application area in this review, followed by network design and location problems. The most frequent hybridization method employed is local search, and new features aim to increase population diversity.\n\nRegarding multi-population approaches specifically, the search results reference work by Gonçalves and Resende from 2012 on \"A parallel multi-population biased random-key genetic algorithm for a container loading problem.\"\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"f982ac10-02b3-4f4e-ae73-643608b60281","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:13.585Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8e6734dc-2db3-4154-98ac-aeb00186550a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6e98e197-7af6-4197-943b-c2c4d744cb5f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a0d2d950c3bbd8398","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GYDrSoUQvWC1QX2fDwo4Ga","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"genetic algorithm\" rectangle placement 70x70 grid scale \"266\" OR \"200 facilities\" feasibility\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Application of Layered Coding Genetic Algorithm in Optimization of Unequal Area Production Facilities Layout - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6607717/\"},{\"title\":\"Application of Layered Coding Genetic Algorithm in Optimization of Unequal Area Production Facilities Layout - Hou - 2019 - Computational Intelligence and Neuroscience - Wiley Online Library\",\"url\":\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1155/2019/3650923\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A Genetic Algorithm For Facility Layout Design In Flexible Manufacturing Systems\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/2373476_A_Genetic_Algorithm_For_Facility_Layout_Design_In_Flexible_Manufacturing_Systems\"},{\"title\":\"New improved hybrid genetic algorithm for optimizing facility layout design of reconfigurable manufacturing system | Scientific Reports\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-97526-x\"},{\"title\":\"A multi objective genetic algorithm for the facility layout problem based upon slicing structure encoding - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0957417412001431\"},{\"title\":\"A new metaheuristic genetic-based placement algorithm for 2D strip packing | Journal of Industrial Engineering International\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s40092-014-0047-9\"},{\"title\":\"A robust genetic algorithm for rectangle packing problem | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/227001808_A_robust_genetic_algorithm_for_rectangle_packing_problem\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Solving facility layout problems with strict geometric constraints using a two-phase genetic algorithm\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/232818282_Solving_facility_layout_problems_with_strict_geometric_constraints_using_a_two-phase_genetic_algorithm\"},{\"title\":\"Improved Genetic Algorithm for the Facility Layout Optimization Problem | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-93965-5_23\"},{\"title\":\"A genetic algorithm for facility layout problems of different manufacturing environments | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/222704118_A_genetic_algorithm_for_facility_layout_problems_of_different_manufacturing_environments\"}]\n\nI found search results related to genetic algorithms for facility layout problems and rectangle packing. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**Rectangle Packing in 70x70 Grid:** One study solved the problem of packing consecutive squares up to 24x24 in a square of size 70x70, which directly matches your grid specification.\n\n**Genetic Algorithm Applications:** Genetic algorithms have shown to be highly efficient in solving facility layout problems due to their ability to reach different areas of the feasible region using its mutation component.\n\n**Feasibility of Solutions:** The approach assumes all facilities are rectangular blocks with a given area, and all facilities must be located in a given area and cannot overlap between them.\n\n**Large-Scale Problems:** A layered coding genetic algorithm method can generate feasible solutions rapidly and can provide larger-scale unequal area facilities layout problem solving.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific information about a \"266\" scale or a \"200 facilities\" benchmark that you mentioned. The research appears to focus on facilities layout problems and rectangle packing, but doesn't specifically reference those exact parameters in the available search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4311e730-f73b-4671-9f11-ff468f76906e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:14.121Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6e98e197-7af6-4197-943b-c2c4d744cb5f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4311e730-f73b-4671-9f11-ff468f76906e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a0d2d950c3bbd8398","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01BEJ8rvzj2XoDq4fFNpJxoo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have sufficient material to provide a comprehensive analysis. Let me consolidate.\n\n---\n\n# 进化算法在 2D 放置/Packing 上的调研报告\n\n## 1. Memetic Algorithm = GA + Local Search\n\nMoscato 1989 提出：把 GA 的全局搜索 + 每个 individual 的 local search 混在一起。GEK & Hahn 2010 的 *Memetic Algorithm for 2D Bin-Packing with Rotations* 是经典工作，操作子专为 packing 设计。Bortfeldt 2006 把 Tabu search 嵌进 GA 解 strip packing。\n\n**跟纯 LNS 的差别：** LNS 是单解 destroy/repair；Memetic 是多解种群 + 每解局部搜索。Memetic 的多样性更高，但每代成本也更高。两者可以叠加——Memetic 的 local search 步骤本身可以是 LNS（NSGA-II + ALNS 已有联合调度论文）。\n\n## 2. 多种群 GA / Island Model\n\nPaliwal & Shankar 2017 *An island model genetic algorithm for unequal area facility layout problems*：6-8 个子种群并行进化，定期迁移精英；解 UA-FLP（最贴近我们工业规划器的问题族）。\n\nSteinhöfel 等 2018 *GPU Implementation of Island Model GA for UA-FLP*：GPU 加速 27x vs 串行 CPU、4.5x vs 传统 island。**对我们 4 进程并行调度有直接借鉴价值**——每个 worker 跑一个 island，迁移频率可控。\n\n## 3. 2D Rectangle Packing 专门编码\n\n主流编码方式（按成熟度排序）：\n- **Sequence Pair (SP)**：Murata 1996 提出，VLSI floorplan 标配。两个 module 序列推导布局，O(n²) 解码。Mumford 2000 *Adaptive GA for VLSI Floorplanning based on Sequence-Pair* 是经典。\n- **Random Keys / BRKGA**：Bean 1994 + Resende，每个 gene 是 [0,1] 随机数，解码器把它转成 placement 顺序 + BLF（bottom-left-fill）。Gonçalves & Resende 2013 *BRKGA for 2D and 3D bin packing*：858 instances，多数对到 optimal，比 branch-and-cut 快 5 个数量级（0.0087s vs 1004s）。\n- **Slicing tree**：guillotine cuts 的二叉树编码。\n- **BLF order**：直接是 placement 顺序的 permutation。\n\n2024-2025 新进展：Zhang 等 2024 SL-VNS（skyline + VNS），Scientific Reports 2025 图像处理 + GA 解 irregular packing。MDPI 2024 *DRL Floorplanning Based on Sequence Pairs* 在 MCNC/GSRC 上超越传统 SP-GA。\n\n## 4. Hyper-heuristic / 算子选择\n\nLópez-Camacho 2014 *Robust hyper-heuristic for offline 2D bin packing*：自动选择 BLF/NFD/FFD 等启发式，跨 instance 泛化能力比单一算子强。Burke 等的 hyper-heuristic 综述把 packing 列为标准应用域。\n\nDE vs PSO vs GA 在 packing 上：DE 适合连续参数（BRKGA 的 random key），PSO 适合 layout 的连续坐标松弛，GA 通用但需要好编码。Asta & Özcan 2024 *DE Hyper-Heuristic for Tuning Parameter Adaptation* 提出自适应混合。\n\n## 5. 进化算法 + CP-SAT 混合\n\n**没找到现成 GA + CP-SAT paper**，但范式清晰：\n- **GA → CP-SAT verify**：GA 找 incumbent，CP-SAT 用 incumbent 做 hint 或 RINS 起点验证最优。这跟我们 RINS warm-start 思路兼容。\n- **GA 用 mini CP-SAT 评估**：每个 individual 调一次受限 CP-SAT 算可行性 + area，但 266 设施单次 CP-SAT 评估就要分钟级，**完全不可行**。\n- **GA + LP 松弛**：MDPI 2023 *Hybrid GA + LP for irregular packing* 是现成工作。\n\nDanna 等 RINS 原始论文明确说：\"advantage of RINS over GA/SA: do not sequentially go through pool, search exponentially-sized space implicitly\"——**RINS 在 MIP 子问题里其实更优**。但有 hybrid：Yaghini 等 2016 *GA Based on RINS in Local Branching Framework*——GA 初始种群用 RINS 解 seed。\n\n## 6. 70×70 + 266 设施可行性\n\n**编码爆炸：** 266 设施 placement permutation = 266! ≈ 10⁵²⁹，比 70×70 grid 的 4900 个格子组合空间还大。直接 permutation GA 收敛极慢。\n\n**BRKGA 编码可行性：** 266 个 [0,1] random keys + skyline/BLF 解码器。每代 100 individuals × 解码 O(266²) ≈ 7M ops/gen，纯 Python 需 ~5s/gen，C++ 后端 <0.1s/gen。1000 代 ≈ 1.5 小时（C++）。\n\n**致命问题：** 我们的目标不是塞满，是 **max_lex(area, min_side) 找空矩形**，且要满足 binding/routing/flow 四层 Benders。GA 解码器需内嵌可行性检查——这正是 CP-SAT 在做的事，绕不过去。\n\n## 7. DEAP / pymoo / PyGAD 框架对比\n\n| 框架 | 成熟度 | 性能 | CP-SAT 集成 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **DEAP** | 最高（10+ 年）| Python loop 慢，需 numpy/numba 加速 | 完全靠手撸 |\n| **pymoo** | 高（多目标 SOTA）| 中等 | 可在 Problem.evaluate 里调 ortools |\n| **PyGAD** | 中（GPU/Keras 友好）| GPU 加速可观 | 集成成本高 |\n| **EvoX** | 新（2024 arxiv）| GPU 分布式最快 | 无 |\n\n**集成成本估计：** pymoo + ortools，写 BRKGA 解码器 + 适应度 ≈ 2-3 周工程量；要做并行 + checkpoint ≈ 再加 1-2 周。\n\n## 8. 学术 SOTA 与 vs CP-SAT 差距\n\n经典 2D bin packing benchmark（Berkey-Wang、Martello-Vigo）上：BRKGA 在中小 instance 多数能匹配 optimal，大 instance（>200 items）通常落后 CP-SAT/Gurobi 1-3%。\n\n**GA 反超 CP-SAT 的场景**：\n- irregular（NFP）packing：CP-SAT 难表达\n- 强多目标 / 模糊约束\n- instance 数 >500 且时间预算 <60s\n\n**我们的场景偏向 CP-SAT 强项**：硬约束多（Benders 四层）、规则确定、目标 lex。**GA 在这里不会反超**。\n\n## 9. GA + ML Hybrid\n\nPreprints 2025 *GNN + GA for Road Networks*：GNN 预测 edge 权重偏好，引导 GA 初始解和变异方向，速度快 3%。X²GNN（ICLR 2025）：unsupervised neural exploration + iterative refinement。Liu 等 2024 *Deep Neural Crossover*：DRL encoder-decoder 选 gene 替代随机 crossover。Reijnen 等 2024 *DRL Adaptive GA for Job Shop*：DRL 选算子 + 调参。\n\n**对我们价值：** 跟 S4/AI sidecar 路线契合（Lane C），但需要先有 GA 框架才能在上面叠 GNN/DRL。\n\n## 10. 跟我们 LNS / RINS 方案的关系\n\n| 维度 | RINS warm-start（已选）| Memetic / BRKGA | 叠加方案 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 工程量 | 小（CP-SAT 内置 hint）| 大（写编码 + 解码 + 算子）| 极大 |\n| 与 Benders 兼容 | 天然 | 需为每层子问题设计 fitness | 困难 |\n| 期望加速 | 1.5-3x（已有论文支撑）| 不确定，可能负收益 | — |\n| 失败回滚 | 关 hint 即可 | 整套删掉 | — |\n\n---\n\n## 可行性评估 + 是否值得 PoC\n\n**结论：不值得做 PoC，至少 Phase 3B 内不做。**\n\n**理由：**\n1. **目标错配**：我们要的是\"对 max_lex(area, min_side) 的认证最优\"，GA/Memetic 输出的是启发式 incumbent，不能替代 CP-SAT 的 proof，只能做 warm-start——而 RINS 已经填了这个位置且工程更轻。\n2. **约束错配**：Benders 四层（master / binding / routing / flow）每层都是硬约束，GA 的 fitness 必须内嵌完整可行性检查；这跟\"调一次 CP-SAT\"等价，没有加速。\n3. **规模错配**：266 设施编码空间 10⁵²⁹，BRKGA 可压到 [0,1]²⁶⁶，但每代解码 + 评估仍需调子 solver，无法摊薄。\n4. **生态错配**：我们用 OR-Tools CP-SAT portfolio（已含 LNS workers + 多种 first-solution 子求解器），CP-SAT 自身就是\"种群式\"。再外挂 GA 是重复造轮子。\n5. **风险错配**：AI Safety Contract 禁止 AI/启发式写 checkpoint、修改证明源，GA 输出只能做 hint，跟 RINS 角色重合。\n\n**只有这两种情况值得回头考虑：**\n- RINS warm-start 实测加速 <1.2x，且 CP-SAT 自带 LNS workers 也榨不出更多\n- 项目转向\"探索性 exploratory 路径\"或非认证 baseline benchmark（CLAUDE.md 明确切断了这条路）\n\n**如果未来要做，建议路线：** pymoo 框架 + BRKGA 编码 + skyline 解码 + island model（4 islands 对齐我们 4 worker），先在 30×30 缩小问题上跑 PoC 对照 CP-SAT，再决定要不要扩到 70×70。预估一次性工程量 4-6 周。\n\n## Sources\n\n- [BRKGA Review (Londe, Pessoa, Andrade, Resende 2025, EJOR)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0377221724002303)\n- [BRKGA Review preprint arxiv 2312.00961](https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.00961)\n- [BRKGA for 2D and 3D bin packing (Gonçalves & Resende 2013)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0925527313001837)\n- [BRKGA 2D Strip Packing with Order/Stability Constraints](https://www.scielo.br/j/pope/a/6rm6JsNbRnLQJrr8YJgbFzk/?lang=en)\n- [Parallel Multi-Population BRKGA for Container Loading](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054811000827)\n- [Memetic Algorithm for 2D Bin-Packing with Rotations (Springer)](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-14883-5_69)\n- [Memetic Algorithm 2D Multi-objective Bin-Packing (ACM GECCO)](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/2001858.2002016)\n- [Effective Evolutionary Algorithm for Rectangles in Circle (EJOR 2025)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0377221725003297)\n- [Optimizing 2D Irregular Packing via Image Processing + CI (Sci Rep 2025)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-97202-0)\n- [Island Model GA for UA-FLP (Paliwal & Shankar)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0957417416305358)\n- [GPU Island Model GA for UA-FLP (MDPI Applied Sciences)](https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3417/8/9/1604)\n- [Adaptive GA for VLSI Floorplanning based on Sequence-Pair (IEEE)](https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/855997/)\n- [DRL Floorplanning Based on Sequence Pairs (MDPI 2024)](https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3417/14/7/2905)\n- [Hybrid RL + GA for VLSI Floorplanning](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/373763040_A_Hybrid_Reinforcement_Learning_and_Genetic_Algorithm_for_VLSI_Floorplanning)\n- [Hybrid GA + LP for 2D Irregular Packing (MDPI 2023)](https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3417/13/22/12474)\n- [Modified GA + Image Processing for Irregular Parts (MDPI Math 2024)](https://www.mdpi.com/2227-7390/12/22/3470)\n- [Hybrid Biased GA for Unequal Rectangles in Circle (COR 2024)](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1016/j.cor.2024.106716)\n- [RINS Original Paper (Danna, Rothberg, Le Pape)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10107-004-0518-7)\n- [GA Based on RINS in Local Branching Framework (Yaghini et al.)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11067-015-9284-8)\n- [Evolutionary Hyper-Heuristics for Bi-Objective 2D Bin Packing](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/315897992_Evolutionary_hyper-heuristics_for_tackling_bi-objective_2D_bin_packing_problems)\n- [Robust Hyper-Heuristics for 2D Bin Packing (López-Camacho)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1568494615004561)\n- [DRL Adaptive GA for Flexible Job Shop Scheduling (2025)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0952197625004476)\n- [Constrained MOO with DRL Operator Selection](https://www.ieee-jas.net/article/doi/10.1109/JAS.2023.123687)\n- [GNN + GA for Combinatorial Road Networks (Preprints 2025)](https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202512.0393)\n- [X²GNN: Explore-Exploit GNN (ICLR 2025)](https://www.cs.cornell.edu/gomes/pdf/2025_acikalin_iclr_x2gnn.pdf)\n- [DRL for 2D Autoclave Packing (Springer 2025)](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-032-05179-0_4)\n- [DEAP framework](https://github.com/DEAP/deap)\n- [pymoo framework](https://pymoo.org/)\n- [EvoX GPU Distributed Framework (arxiv 2301.12457)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2301.12457)\n- [CP-SAT Primer (Krupke)](https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer)\n- [Memetic Algorithm Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memetic_algorithm)\n- [Hexaly LNS reference](https://www.hexaly.com/algorithms/large-neighborhood-search-lns)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2957,"cache_read_input_tokens":39417,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2957,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosPoxe98e5HmzKW9P6g","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"9f364c88-2f5c-4b83-bcdb-dadbf96f66a8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:52.180Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
